  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_2d93a74fcdb14b8e84411f75f868c950",
      "statement": "OpenWiki Service accepts a public Git URL, a private one plus a personal access token, or an uploaded zip/tar, and returns the documentation generated by the OpenWiki CLI as a downloadable wiki.zip (Markdown plus openwiki/.claims/), optionally committing that wiki back to the source repository when push is requested.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L1-L7",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:baf5e46a6df90a9bf165bfb6a1b073667e36f488bf0207e8c786dc7220d14385:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/main.py#L75-L85",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4625755cbf7d1e8e66601a172c5e1526ffba301b8a3f1616eba298fbf2012720:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ff8d9bbb48994fd9898543d0662c16ab",
      "statement": "The API process never generates documentation: it only enqueues wikis, serves status/logs/zip and requeues stale claims, while generation runs in separate worker containers of the same image started with `python -m app.worker`; the two sides communicate solely through the shared data volume (openwiki.db for coordination plus jobs/<wiki_id>/ for workspace, logs and artifacts).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L9-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bde427a81803e461c3afe7247a748f69111b73df6086715fb0724e1903661a59:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/main.py#L1-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4c8aec0ba536fb901bbb87779e7315156dd6d5d0fc7800d4dbcc9981d9190973:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/worker/__main__.py#L1-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:60b30b18270269ecd191de075043a5681542597d50f8bd95c31119c5608c8bc1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fdb2b90f5e604517b026fe3407029a60",
      "statement": "Worker concurrency comes from replicas rather than from threads: each worker container runs MAX_CONCURRENT_JOBS generations (default 1, wired to the compose worker service), so horizontal scaling is `docker compose up -d --scale worker=N`, and the compose worker service disables its healthcheck while only the API exposes one.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L55-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9b7c59731368b6b1a5f745279a514db24b8e8f2d024c54c988de36abf4400fa5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docker-compose.yml#L21-L38",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:106b23850fcdefa7a4936b0284bb108d5f53daf09e96b43c48fe459a4b4cea75:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2aa61bea08744688b858f0558bcb1c3e",
      "statement": "Setting RUN_LOCAL_WORKER=true makes create_app start a WorkerLoop inside the API process, which is the single-container/dev mode and the same loop the worker containers use; the started worker (and its optional header-injecting proxy) is exposed on app.state so it can be stopped during lifespan shutdown.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/main.py#L53-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b5d5e0ab27eb481c512218f615ac4f9623140ea2e5cfc24f8ad661ae6877982e:"
